{"route":"hyperlinks","routeLabel":"Hyperlink entries","scriptId":"0094","lineCount":181,"lines":[{"ref":"saihate:hyperlinks:0094:000010","line":10,"sourceId":"0094:000010","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","japanese":"　それはある晴れた昼下がり―――","english":"It was a sunny afternoon—","hyperlinks":[],"japaneseHyperlinks":[]},{"ref":"saihate:hyperlinks:0094:000011","line":11,"sourceId":"0094:000011","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","japanese":"　四人は葬式饅頭を食していた。","english":"The four of them were eating funeral buns.","hyperlinks":[],"japaneseHyperlinks":[]},{"ref":"saihate:hyperlinks:0094:000013","line":13,"sourceId":"0094:000013","speakerJa":"章二","speakerEn":"Shouji","japanese":"「……最近、葬式増えたなぁ」","english":"“...There've been a lot of funerals lately.”","hyperlinks":[],"japaneseHyperlinks":[]},{"ref":"saihate:hyperlinks:0094:000014","line":14,"sourceId":"0094:000014","speakerJa":"忍","speakerEn":"Shinobu","japanese":"「おかげでおやつに不自由しない」","english":"“At least we never run short of snacks.”","hyperlinks":[],"japaneseHyperlinks":[]},{"ref":"saihate:hyperlinks:0094:000016","line":16,"sourceId":"0094:000016","speakerJa":"沙也加","speakerEn":"Sayaka","japanese":"「不謹慎」","english":"“That's in poor taste.”","hyperlinks":[],"japaneseHyperlinks":[]},{"ref":"saihate:hyperlinks:0094:000018","line":18,"sourceId":"0094:000018","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","japanese":"　沙也加の親戚が亡くなった。\n　大往生だったため塞ぐところのない葬式だった。","english":"One of Sayaka's relatives had died. The relative had lived to a ripe old age, so it was hardly a somber funeral.","hyperlinks":[],"japaneseHyperlinks":[]},{"ref":"saihate:hyperlinks:0094:000019","line":19,"sourceId":"0094:000019","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","japanese":"　葬式饅頭が余ったので、列席した中で一番若い沙\n也加に押しつけられた。","english":"There were funeral buns left over, so they were foisted on Sayaka, the youngest person in attendance.","hyperlinks":[],"japaneseHyperlinks":[]},{"ref":"saihate:hyperlinks:0094:000021","line":21,"sourceId":"0094:000021","speakerJa":"章二","speakerEn":"Shouji","japanese":"「確かに風が吹けば葬式饅頭